  "prefLabel": "Ec-Wtr 203.02 Preliminary Notice of Appeal (PNA) and Offer to Enter Into Settlement Discussions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ec-Wtr 203.02 Preliminary Notice of Appeal (PNA) and Offer to Enter Into Settlement Discussions.\n\n(a) Any person who wishes to file a preliminary notice of appeal (PNA) and offers to enter into settlement discussions shall file a PNA in accordance with this section and RSA 21-O:14, I-b.\n\n(b) The PNA shall:\n\n(1) Conform to the filing requirements of Ec-Wtr 201.01;\n\n(2) Conform to the PNA requirements of RSA 21-O:14, I-b; and\n\n(3) Be clearly marked “Attention: Appeals Clerk” on the envelope.\n\n(c) The appellant shall serve the notice of the PNA either in person or via certified mail and in accordance with RSA 21-O:14, I-b (b).\n\n(d) Any party providing notice to the preliminary appellant in accordance with RSA 21-O:14, I-b(d) shall submit a copy of the notice to the appeals clerk by submitting a filing that conforms to the requirements of Ec-Wtr 201.01.\n\n(e) A notice of appeal filed pursuant to RSA 21-O:14, I-b(e) shall comply with Ec-Wtr 203.01.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note # 1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Ec-Wtr 200) #13923, eff 4-11-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ec-wtr200.html"
